# Netlify response headers.
#
# WHY THERE IS NO CSP ON THE WILDCARD /* RULE
#   Netlify MERGES (appends), it does not replace, headers when more than one
#   rule matches a path. A Content-Security-Policy in /* would therefore be
#   emitted ALONGSIDE the page-specific CSP below, and browsers enforce the
#   INTERSECTION (the most restrictive) of multiple CSP headers. That made the
#   strict wildcard policy keep clamping the pages that need a looser one — it
#   blocked the AI Lab's jsDelivr/Hugging Face downloads and the contact form's
#   form-action 'self'. So /* carries ONLY the singleton security headers
#   (which are identical on every page and safe to set once), and every HTML
#   page gets its OWN complete CSP. No CSP combining can occur.
#
# CSP TIERS (each page below uses exactly one):
#   - Standard: content pages. script-src self + cdnjs; form-action 'none';
#     connect-src lists only CDN hosts, never 'self'.
#   - Contact (/contact, /contact.html): Standard, but form-action 'self' so the
#     native (no-JS) Netlify form POST is allowed. connect-src still omits 'self'.
#   - Builder/Verify (/app*, /verify*): Standard. form-action 'none' and no
#     connect-src 'self' — a script on an evidence page has nowhere on the
#     allowlist to POST message content. This is the no-egress privacy promise.
#   - AI Lab (/ai-lab, /ai-lab.html): BOTH the Transformers.js bundle
#     (js/ai/vendor/transformers.min.js) AND the executable ONNX runtime loader
#     glue (js/ai/vendor/ort-wasm-simd-threaded.jsep.mjs) are VENDORED locally and
#     imported from our own origin, so NO external JavaScript executes in the same
#     page context as pasted messages. script-src is therefore 'self' only (plus
#     'wasm-unsafe-eval' + blob: for the WebAssembly runtime — the vendored
#     bundle and ONNX glue use WebAssembly.instantiate(Streaming) with no eval()
#     or new Function(), so 'unsafe-eval' is deliberately NOT granted) and
#     does NOT include cdn.jsdelivr.net. connect-src adds jsDelivr + Hugging Face
#     for GET-only BINARY downloads — the ONNX wasm binary (jsDelivr) and the model
#     weights (Hugging Face), data that runs in the wasm sandbox, never page script.
#     connect-src still OMITS 'self', so there is no POST path back to our origin.
#   - Contact success (/contact-success, /contact-success.html): standard tier.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()

/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://fonts.googleapis.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

